[00:54.00] I went down to St. James in Firm Rain
[01:00.00] Saw my baby there
[01:04.00] Stretched out on a long white table
[01:09.00] So sweet, so cold, so fair
[01:13.00] Let her go, let her go, God bless her
[01:18.00] Wherever she may be
[01:22.00] She can look this wide world over
[01:27.00] She'll never find a sweet man like me
[01:31.00] When I die I want you to dress me in straight lace shoes
[01:36.00] Fox, backcoat, and steps and hats
[01:40.00] Put a twenty dollar gold piece on my watch chain
[01:45.00] So the boys will know I died standing past
